@startuml
title Proposed in-Rholang Module/ Theory declaration flow
left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam rectangle {
  BorderColor #37474F
  FontColor #102027
  RoundCorner 16
}

rectangle "Rholang source\nModule / Theory\nBNFC Reg and typed builders" as source #DCEEFF
rectangle "Generated Rholang\nparser and Ddl AST" as frontend #BBDEFB
rectangle "Structural declaration\nelaboration" as elaborate #B3E5FC
database "Canonical value\nand LanguageCore" as core #C8E6C9
rectangle "Exact-core Data\nprogrammatic input" as data #E1F5FE
rectangle "Existing lexer / WPDA\nimage compiler" as parser #D1C4E9
rectangle "Existing OSLF\nsemantic-image compiler" as semantic #D1C4E9
rectangle "Independent capability\ngrant and policy" as grant #FFE0B2
rectangle "Atomic installation\nand verification" as install #FFF9C4
rectangle "Opaque installed handle\nFLT parse / match / reduce / observe" as runtime #FFCDD2

source --> frontend
frontend --> elaborate
elaborate --> core
data --> core
core --> parser
core --> semantic
parser --> install
semantic --> install
grant --> install
install --> runtime

note bottom of elaborate
  No source-text DDL reparse.
  Native BNFC Reg is parsed structurally.
end note
note bottom of install
  Requested rights do not grant authority.
end note
@enduml
